notes               = "Untitled in source. A rubâ'i: lines 1, 2 and 4 carry the mono-rhyme -âni (هجرانی / حیرانی / بارانی) and line 3 runs free — the classical quatrain scheme. The diction is deliberately old (هجران, the ghazal's separation; حیرانی, the Sufi's bewilderment) and the image deliberately plain: a man walking wet streets with his eyes shut. ۱۳۶۸/۵/۱ is 1 Mordad, a summer month, so the Gregorian half is 1989 (+621). Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

سَرم به شانهٔ تو با نوای هجرانی
بلندی نَفَسم پُر ز عطرِ حیرانی
دو چشم بسته‌ام و در هوای گرییدن
عبور می‌کنم از کوچه‌های بارانی
۱۳۶۸/۵/۱

===machine===

My head on your shoulder, with the strain of parting
The rise of my breath full of the scent of bewilderment
Both eyes closed, and in the mood for weeping
I pass through the rainy alleys
1368/5/1

===lantern===

My head on your shoulder, a parting-air playing,
my breath drawn long and full of the scent of bewilderment.
Both eyes shut, and in a mood to weep,
I pass on through the rainy alleys.

1368/5/1

